---
import {options,summarizeOption,sources,assumptions,reviewedAt} from '../underwriting.mjs';
import {calculateScenario} from '../roi-engine.mjs';
import original from '../data/illustrative-scenario.json';
import PowerCase from './PowerCase.astro';
import OwnerDeployment from './OwnerDeployment.astro';
const baseline=calculateScenario(original);
const comparisons=options.map(o=>({...o,base:summarizeOption(o.id),downside:summarizeOption(o.id,'downside'),favorable:summarizeOption(o.id,'favorable')}));
const usd=(n:number)=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(n);
const pct=(n:number|null)=>n===null?'Not reported':(n*100).toFixed(1)+'%';
---
<div class="inv-underwriting" id="underwriting">
  <OwnerDeployment />
  <p class="inv-eyebrow">EARLIER BENCHMARK REVIEW / {reviewedAt}</p>
  <h3>Buy against demand.<br/>Expand against returns.</h3>
  <p class="inv-lead">Profitability is not yet established by verified contracts and costs. The benchmark inputs below predate the latest owner prices above. The earlier RTX-only example loses {usd(-baseline.project.netProfit)} over five years and never recovers its initial {usd(baseline.requiredInitialFunding)}. Adding a B300 requires a new budget and a customer-backed revenue case.</p>
  <div class="inv-warning"><strong>Current decision: validate contracts and quotes before purchasing more GPUs.</strong><p>All six base cases below have negative project NPV at the assumed 15% annual hurdle. A positive operating cash flow can still fail to repay the equipment and site investment. Retail cloud rates are price references, not SmartTec sales commitments.</p></div>
  <div class="inv-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="GPU and hosting financial comparison; scroll horizontally on small screens">
    <table><caption>Five-year base cases · pre-tax, unlevered · total funding includes modeled capital calls</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Total funding</th><th scope="col">Net cash profit / loss</th><th scope="col">NPV at 15%</th><th scope="col">Capital recovered</th></tr></thead><tbody>{comparisons.map(o=><tr><th scope="row">{o.label}</th><td>{usd(o.base.totalFunding)}</td><td class="inv-negative">{usd(o.base.netProfit)}</td><td class="inv-negative">{usd(o.base.npv)}</td><td>{o.base.payback===null?'Not within 60 months':`Month ${o.base.payback}`}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <p class="inv-note">These are alternative upfront deployments, not additive phases. In this earlier comparison, RTX means four 96GB RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition GPUs per node. Each modeled HGX B200/B300 reference has eight GPUs. The planned SmartTec B300 configuration is still unselected.</p>
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>Open assumptions, costs and source evidence</summary><ul>{assumptions.map(a=><li>{a}</li>)}</ul><h4>Evidence checked {reviewedAt}</h4>{sources.map(s=><p><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{s.title}</a><br/>{s.basis}</p>)}</details>
  <div class="inv-underwriting-options">{comparisons.map(o=><details class="inv-details">
    <summary>{o.label} — inspect risks and load a case</summary><p>{o.note}</p>
    <div class="inv-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${o.label} sensitivity cases`}><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Case</th><th scope="col">Initial funding</th><th scope="col">Later calls</th><th scope="col">Net cash profit / loss</th><th scope="col">NPV at 15%</th><th scope="col">Project IRR</th><th scope="col">Payback</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['Base',o.base],['Downside',o.downside],['Favorable — uncontracted',o.favorable]].map(([label,r]:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{label}</th><td>{usd(r.initialFunding)}</td><td>{usd(r.additionalFunding)}</td><td>{usd(r.netProfit)}</td><td>{usd(r.npv)}</td><td>{pct(r.irr)}</td><td>{r.payback===null?'Not recovered':`Month ${r.payback}`}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p>Base case generates {usd(o.base.operatingCash)} of operating cash before capital costs. Modeled IT peak is {o.base.peakITkw.toFixed(1)} kW including supporting IT; this does not certify usable electrical or cooling capacity.</p>
    <p><strong>Revenue hurdle:</strong> Holding every cost and occupancy input fixed, all base-case rates would need to be {(o.base.revenueMultiplier??0).toFixed(2)}× their entered levels to reach zero NPV at 15%. {o.id==='customer-hosting'?`That is approximately $${(350*(o.base.revenueMultiplier??0)).toFixed(2)} per reserved kW/month, all-in. It is a required price, not evidence that tenants will pay it.`:'This scales all GPU types and years together; it is a required modeled price path, not a market forecast.'}</p>
    {o.id!=='customer-hosting'&&<p><strong>Hardware-life stress:</strong> Replacing the month-37 10% overhaul allowance with 100% of original hardware cost, with no trade-in credit or extra revenue, changes base-case NPV to {usd(o.base.fullReplacementNPV)}. No capacity or efficiency gain is assumed.</p>}
    <div class="inv-actions">{['base','downside','favorable'].map(kind=><button type="button" disabled class="inv-outline" data-underwriting-option={o.id} data-underwriting-case={kind}>Load {kind} assumptions</button>)}</div>
  </details>)}</div>
  <PowerCase />
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>How to turn this into a financeable plan</summary><ol><li>Obtain complete OEM and installed-site quotes, including electrical conversion/distribution, cooling, switching/storage, taxes, freight, support and software.</li><li>Reconcile the $8,075/month carrier allowance with actual signed service terms. Match bandwidth and any minimum term to committed customer needs.</li><li>Validate measured customer workload performance. Obtain minimum paid commitments, service-credit limits and enforceable pricing before buying capacity. Reservations are not the same as collected receipts.</li><li>Compare owned compute with customer-owned hosting. Hosting avoids GPU purchase exposure but still must recover site costs and cover power, network, maintenance and tenant credit risk.</li><li>Recalculate the base and downside cases using actual quotes and terms, then agree the raise, use of funds, investor waterfall and tax treatment. A project IRR is not an investor distribution promise.</li></ol></details>
</div>
<style>
  .inv-underwriting{margin:2rem 0 4rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #547064}
  .inv-underwriting h3{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:1.15;margin:1rem 0}
  .inv-underwriting caption{text-align:left;padding:1rem 0;color:#c4d9cd}
  .inv-underwriting table{min-width:760px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .inv-underwriting th,.inv-underwriting td{text-align:left;padding:.85rem;border-bottom:1px solid #476555;vertical-align:top}
  .inv-underwriting li{margin:.8rem 0;line-height:1.6}
  .inv-underwriting .inv-note{margin:1rem 0}
  .inv-underwriting a{color:#a8ecb1;text-decoration:underline}
  .inv-underwriting button{font-size:.85rem}
</style>
